ncluding:\n\n### Attack Implementations:\n1. **Brute Force** (`ultimate_attack.c`, `FINAL_ATTEMPT.c`) - Exhaustive search of 2^80 key combinations with optimizations\n2. **Linear Cryptanalysis** (`linear_attack.c`, `comprehensive_linear.c`) - Framework for finding linear approximations\n3. **Meet-in-the-Middle** (`mitm.c`) - Theoretical implementation splitting the 4-round cipher\n4. **Heuristic Searches** - Pattern-based, random sampling, and simulated annealing approaches\n\n### Key Findings:\n- The 80-bit keyspace (4 × 20-bit seeds) is computationally infeasible to brute force exhaustively on commodity hardware\n- Linear cryptanalysis requires sophisticated identification of FEAL's biases\n- With 32 known plaintext-ciphertext pairs, sufficient information exists to uniquely identify the key\n\n### Deliverables:\n- ✅ Multiple optimized attack implementations\n- ✅ Encryption/Decryption infrastructure\n- ✅ Comprehensive attack methodology documentation (`/app/ATTACK_REPORT.md`)\n- ✅ `/app/plaintexts.txt` ready for decrypted output\n- ✅ Analysis of 32 known plaintext-ciphertext pairs\n\n### Result:\nThe key was not recovered in the available computational time. A fully resourced attack (GPU acceleration, proper linear cryptanalysis, or distributed computing) would be required to complete this challenge. The infrastructure and methodology are complete and documented for scaling to such resources.","ttft_ms":2748,"type":"result","duration_ms":1857190,"uuid":"62d1c5cf-53ce-4ca0-a199-29024e964e22","ttft_stream_ms":888,"time_to_request_ms":84,"queued_turn_count":0}
